1
00:00:03,202 --> 00:00:05,770
A winter reading circle gathers around one

2
00:00:05,770 --> 00:00:08,522
thick hardback, seen from its gilt fore-edge.

3
00:00:09,506 --> 00:00:13,560
Each silk ribbon marks where a reader sits in the book,

4
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:17,466
tinted by whether they are ahead, on pace, or behind.

5
00:00:18,281 --> 00:00:21,490
Pages past the fog line fall into shade, showing

6
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:25,101
the spoiler-safe horizon of the slowest active reader.

7
00:00:25,908 --> 00:00:29,548
Switching to the Pace lens overlays today’s expected

8
00:00:29,548 --> 00:00:32,488
page band and each reader’s catch-up time.

9
00:00:33,294 --> 00:00:36,125
The Notes lens highlights open margin slips and

10
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:38,654
sealed flaps for chapters not yet reached.

11
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:42,465
The Today panel focuses the next meeting flag

12
00:00:42,465 --> 00:00:45,197
and shows how many effective days remain.

13
00:00:46,006 --> 00:00:52,386
Toggling View As switches between the convenor overview and a reader’s spoiler-locked perspective.

14
00:00:53,187 --> 00:00:55,748
In Bookmark, a reader logs their current page

15
00:00:55,748 --> 00:00:58,537
and reading minutes to slide their ribbon deeper.

16
00:00:59,348 --> 00:01:02,790
Progress is saved immediately, and backwards entries are

17
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:05,618
refused unless they are a same-day correction.

18
00:01:06,427 --> 00:01:09,155
In Margin, notes from later chapters stay sealed

19
00:01:09,155 --> 00:01:11,827
until your bookmark passes their starting page.

20
00:01:12,629 --> 00:01:15,906
Reading Plan gives the convenor effective-day pacing

21
00:01:15,906 --> 00:01:19,119
with half-weight weekends and a readiness forecast.

22
00:01:19,923 --> 00:01:22,952
Meeting Pack compiles printable discussion questions and

23
00:01:22,952 --> 00:01:24,683
shows who will be ready on time.

24
00:01:25,491 --> 00:01:27,556
Every reader moves at their own pace,

25
00:01:27,556 --> 00:01:30,291
while the circle stays together without spoilers.

26
00:01:31,093 --> 00:01:34,273
Fore-Edge — built on Microsoft Fabric Apps.
